  "question": "A flywheel starts from rest with a constant angular acceleration and reaches $20$ rad/s in $5$ s. Find the number of revolutions it makes in this time, rounded to the nearest whole number.",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [],
  "answer": "",
  "numerical_answer": "8",
  "tolerance": "0",
  "solution": "$$\\theta = \\frac{\\omega_0 + \\omega}{2}t = \\frac{0 + 20}{2}(5) = 50\\ \\text{rad}$$\n$$\\text{Revolutions} = \\frac{50}{2\\pi} \\approx 7.96 \\approx 8$$",
